  "body": "## What changed\n\nWith \"Pass starts at: Outside\", a later pass of 2D Offset or 2D Pocket (Waterline or Offset rings) that starts at a dead end now enters by a ramp along its own pass. Before, it entered by a plunge or a helix into uncut stock (#3567).\n\n**Maintainer decision** (issue #3567, 2026-11-22): \"At a dead end of a later pass of 2D Offset with \"Pass starts at: Outside\", the tool enters with **a ramp along the pass**.\" The coordinator's standing-word decision (#3567, 23:24Z) accepts the ramp at the ramp angle and names the ramp angle as the control of the load.\n\n**The entry.**\n- `level_order::order` marks each later pass of an Outside plan that no lead-in reaches (`LevelPlan::ramp_starts`).\n- `ladder_links::pass_link` calls `level_ramp_entry::dead_end_ramp` first. At a marked start, the tool goes down by the existing ramp fallback: the zig-zag along the start of the pass (`descent::ramp_fallback`).\n- The ramp angle is the entry's ramp angle, or 3 degrees (`links::DEFAULT_RAMP_ANGLE`) when the operation sets none. The leg limit is the entry's maximum ramp length.\n- The ramp starts at the material top of the level plus the plunge height. The last leg lands on the pass start at depth. The pass then cuts the ramped stretch again at the floor.\n- The ramp lead is thinned by Douglas-Peucker within `ARC_FIT_TOL` (0.01 mm). Each kept point is a vertex of the pass.\n\n## Review items (review of e7ae538a3)\n\n1. **No silent plunge.** `level_ramp_entry::too_short_at` checks each dead end at the deepest descent of any cut level. A dead end that is too short for the ramp sends the area to the Auto order with `StartSide::ramp_fallback_note`. That note carries `RINGS_FALLBACK`, so the op raises `Warning::StrategyFallback`. If the ladder still cannot plan the ramp, it names that on the path. Pinned by `a_dead_end_too_short_for_the_ramp_falls_back_to_pure_auto`, `a_dead_end_too_short_for_the_ramp_is_found` and `the_ramp_fallback_note_is_a_rings_fallback`.\n2. **Slope law in the pin.** `late_entry_cut` counts a descending feed as a ramp only when it is at or under the ramp angle plus 0.05 degrees and on the pass path (within 0.02 mm of a floor feed). A steeper feed counts like a plunge (`a_steep_straight_feed_is_not_a_ramp`). The pin asserts that a ramp ran. New pins:\n   - `outside_dead_end_entries_are_no_steeper_than_the_ramp_angle`\n   - `outside_floor_under_each_dead_end_ramp_is_cut`\n   - `outside_dead_end_ramps_width_reading_of_the_stepover_band` (it reads the band width; it is not a proof against a full-width cut)\n3. **A replaced entry is named.** When the ramp replaces the user's Plunge, Helix or Arc entry, the path says so one time, in the #2265 stand-in form (`level_ramp_entry::stand_in_note`, pinned by `a_replaced_entry_is_named`).\n4. **The trigger.** Only marked dead ends get the ramp. The first entry of each level and the ring 0 pieces keep the entry of main: a helix or a plunge into solid stock at the first entry is normal and outside this issue. The Auto-order plan after a completeness-guard fallback has no marks, so it stays pure Auto (pinned byte for byte by `a_dead_end_too_short_for_the_ramp_falls_back_to_pure_auto`). The ladder does not scan the earlier moves with `plunge_law::into_solid` at each pass link.\n5. **The ramp, in plain words.** The ramp is an entry into uncut stock at a dead end. Where the ring cut before does not reach the dead end, the ramp cuts a slot at nearly the full tool width, at the ramp angle. After the ramp, the pass cuts at one stepover. The ramp angle is the control. Measured on the band of the pins (tool D8, stepover 4):\n   - About 25 percent of the tool disc (about 12.6 mm2 of 50.3 mm2) is uncut stock at the start of each of the 8 ramps.\n   - The band width during the ramps is 4.78 mm at most, under the limit of 5.375 mm.\n   - The earlier \"83 percent\" number was the stock that each helix of main cut over its whole orbit (332.88 mm2 / 8 = 41.6 mm2), not the stock in the disc at the start.\n   - Each ramp runs at 3.000 degrees from Z 2.0 to Z -3.0 over 95.41 mm along the pass.\n   - The decision file `docs/decisions/3567-ramp-entry-at-dead-end.md` says this and quotes the two decisions.\n6. **`levels.rs` does not grow.** It has 456 lines (459 on main). The builders are in the new module `level_ramp_entry.rs`.\n7. **The file collision with #3566.** This PR keeps `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement.rs` and moves its grid to `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement/grid.rs`. #3566 must drop its copy, or take its four sibling pins onto this file after this PR merges.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The late-entry pin `outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock`: 332.88 mm2 on main, 0.00 mm2 with the ramp.\n- `pass_start_levels`: 7 of 7, with no limit changed.\n\n## The slow pin is a test-speed problem, not a block\n\nThe verification of `fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge` is slow. It is a test-speed problem, filed as #3587 (`P5`). The verifier speed is filed as #3588 (fix PR #3595, draft). Neither issue blocks #3577.\n\nReadings on this head (`d41c2b76a`):\n- `pocket_pass_start`: 5 passed of 6. The sixth test, `fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge`, did not complete. It stopped at 29 min 23 s. The earlier run tripped the 15-min stall watchdog at 961 s.\n- Every other suite is green:\n  - motion `pass_start_engagement` 6/6, `pass_start_levels` 7/7;\n  - motion lib `machining2d` 267 passed and 10 ignored, `level_ramp_entry` 4/4;\n  - app `offset_pass_start` 4/4, `golden_cl` 33/33, `conformance` 7/7, `adaptive_pass_start` 4/4, `bore_pass_start` 3/3;\n  - the catalogs 37/1/1;\n  - clippy clean;\n  - the light lane 2 twins green.\n\nWhere the time goes (temporary timers, removed):\n- The motion plan and emit take 0.21 s (8850 moves).\n- In the verifier (`camcraft_sim::verify::verify_bodies`), tangency takes 34.7 s for 2232 ramp moves. `reach::band_reach` does not finish in more than 3 minutes.\n- Each ramp move ends at its own Z. The verifier cuts a new slice of the model at each distinct Z (`Rest::islands_at`). `band_reach` adds the boundary samples of each slice to one sample set and tests each move against all of them.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe readings above are the gate of this head. The pinning tests are in `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement.rs`. The motion lib pins are in `level_ramp_entry`, `pass_start`, `level_rings` and `level_order`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine run. No posted G-code was read on a controller.\n- No release-build run time of the fig8 Outside pocket.\n- Adaptive with Outside keeps its old entry at dead ends.\n- No heavy lane (P2, AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset and 2D Pocket Outside: a later pass that starts at a dead end now enters by a ramp along the pass at the entry's ramp angle (3 degrees by default), not by a plunge or helix into uncut stock. At a dead end, the worst sampled start cuts with about 25 percent of the tool disc in uncut stock (12.6 mm2 of 50.3 mm2 for the 4.780 mm band), so the zig-zag cuts a slot at nearly full tool width at 3 degrees. A dead end too short for the ramp cuts the area in the Auto order, and the path names it.\n\nRefs #3353\nRefs #3566\nRefs #3587\nRefs #3588\nFixes #3567\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
